e the race at Likely/Safe D or better", "Markets price the Democrat at ~94%"], "rationale": "The fundamentals, ratings consensus, and prediction markets all point the same way, and the Republican nominee's chaotic primary win and weak fundraising leave little path to an upset. A modest incumbent-plus-money edge over the baseline is justified, but not beyond the evidence.", "watch": "Any late surge of outside Republican spending or a polling miss by the incumbent could narrow the margin, though the GOP nominee's campaign suspension makes that unlikely.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Kristen McDonald Rivet (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Kristen McDonald Rivet, a first-term Democratic incumbent in a district that leans slightly Republican, is heavily favored. She has raised over $5.6 million and holds $4.3 million on hand, while Republican nominee Thomas Smith has raised under $250,000 and drew no outside support. Smith won the GOP primary in August despite having suspended his campaign, defeating a Trump-endorsed rival, and has since skipped debate forums and faced scrutiny over a controversial social media post amplified by his account.\n\nEvery major expert rating places the race at Likely D or stronger, and prediction markets price the Democrat around 94 percent. With no public polling available, the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings, and money, all of which favor the incumbent decisively.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9646, "margin": 12.11}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9589, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9779, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9667, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9568, "margin": 13.0}]}